--- body ---
## Context
`gaze`, `review-pr`, `review-pr-prose`, `verify-adherence`, `verify-gate` are
the five `context: fork` skills and pin their seats to `model-level: standard`
("reviewers stay below the coder tier"). A fork runs at the caller's tier and
cannot judge at launch. Decision: the decorrelation rule applies to the SEATS a
fork launches, not to the fork itself; no concrete `model:` in skill
frontmatter.

## Scope
- Replace the tier pins with the cross-family rule of 1065, including its
  default (one cross-family detached seat, else `no report` and `DEGRADED`).
- `review-pr`'s detached-seat section keeps "record `no report`, never simulate".
- Same PR: retire `tests/test_model_rightsizing.py:56-65` (the fork-frontmatter check).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] None of the five skills declares `model-level` or `effort`
- [ ] The fork-frontmatter test is retired in this PR; the suite passes
- [ ] `make skills-catalog` and `make check-skills-drift` pass
- [ ] `make check` passes
